<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Schleswig</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Southern Jutland</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Schleswig is a historical region and former duchy in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jutland">Jutland</a>, divided since a plebiscite of 1920 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> (North Schleswig) and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> (South Schleswig). Ruled by Danish royal princes and from 1386 by the counts of Holstein, it was joined with Holstein under King Christian I in 1460. Rival Danish and German claims led to the Schleswig Wars of 1848–1851 and 1864, after which it passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/schleswig.jpg" alt="Schleswig" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tinkaer1991 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Duchy_of_Schleswig-Holstein_18th_century.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
